    "result": {
      "ok": true,
      "stdout": "Search assets by type and natural-language intent.\r\n\r\nAGENT QUICKSTART (driving this as an agent? start here):\r\n  Browse commands:  lyra-cli <domain> --help\r\n\r\nUSAGE:\r\n  lyra-cli <domain> <[subdomain] ...> <action> [--flags] [--options]\r\n\r\n\r\nOPTIONS:\r\n  -h, --help                            Print this help message and exit\r\n      --type TEXT REQUIRED              Material search type key. Supported values are listed in\r\n                                        SUPPORTED SEARCH TYPES below.\r\n      --prompt TEXT REQUIRED            Search intent. It can be a word, phrase, or sentence, for example\r\n                                        a style, object, mood, scene, music, or sound description.\r\n      --limit INT:POSITIVE              Maximum number of results to return. Default is 10.\r\n      --need-recommend                  Enable recommendation-augmented ranking for the search results.\r\n      --filter-commercial               Restrict results to commercially usable assets.\r\n      --filter-ai-transition            Filter out AI transition results whose metadata marks\r\n                                        transition_type=ai_transition.\r\n      --search-scene <search-scene>     Visual/audio search scene, for example `vimo_caption`.\r\n      --category-list <category-list>   Comma-separated material category IDs for category-scoped search,\r\n                                        for example `2066,2067`.\r\n      --channel <online|test|local_test> \r\n                                        Material request channel. Use `test` or `local_test` for internal\r\n                                        test resources.\r\n  -v, --version                         Show version information and exit.\r\n      --jq TEXT                         Pretty-print JSON output; with an optional selector like\r\n                                        .result.items[0].id, output the selected JSON value instead of\r\n                                        the full schema envelope.\r\n\r\nWHEN TO USE\r\n  - The user names an exact material, song, filter, effect, sticker, or template.\r\n  - The target is an exact song, music/BGM style, visual asset, sound effect, template, or named material.\r\n  - Topic browsing returned no useful candidates.\r\n\r\nSEARCH INTENT\r\n  Keep the prompt material-native: object, mood, scene, style, motion, instrument,\r\n  tempo, texture, or sound mechanism. Avoid pasting a full editing request as the prompt.\r\n\r\nSUPPORTED SEARCH TYPES\r\n  template, music, sticker, effect, filter, transition, text_template,\r\n  sound, font, flower, subtitle_template, photo, video,\r\n  material_package, emoji_sticker, lyric_animation, anim_text,\r\n  anim_sticker, anim_video, curve_speed, digital_human_template,\r\n  digital_human_background, digital_human_model, face_effect,\r\n  face_sticker, auto_face, auto_makeup, matting_stroke,\r\n  mix_mode, material_lib, style, tone, video_mask,\r\n  voice_change\r\n\r\nEXAMPLES\r\n  $ lyra-cli material search --type sticker --prompt \"cute cat\" --limit 5\r\n  $ lyra-cli material search --type music --prompt \"warm acoustic vlog\" --limit 5\r\n  $ lyra-cli material search --type sound --prompt \"camera shutter\" --limit 5\r\n  $ lyra-cli material search --type effect --prompt \"film grain\" --filter-commercial\r\n  # Search local test material resources.\r\n  $ lyra-cli material search --type sticker --prompt \"local test asset\" --channel test\r\n  # Search a specific animation category.\r\n  $ lyra-cli material search --type anim_text --prompt \"fade in\" --category-list 2066 --search-scene vimo_caption\r\n\r\nOUTPUT\r\n  Returns result.items[].resource_id for query, download, or draft handoff.\r\n",
      "stderr": "",
